WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.560
Add mature nerve growth factor, or NGF, to cultured sympathetic neurons, and they

2
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.020
survive. Now add the same protein before an enzyme has trimmed it.

3
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.880
In Barbara Hempstead's experiments, those neurons died.

4
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.180
How can one factor carry opposite messages?

5
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.720
The answer lies in the receptors on the neuron.

6
00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:28.703
A neuron reads a neurotrophin through two kinds of receptor.

7
00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:34.503
The first kind is the Trk receptors, said "track", and there are three of them.

8
00:00:35.043 --> 00:00:39.703
Each prefers particular factors, and NGF prefers TRAC -A.

9
00:00:40.243 --> 00:00:43.703
The factor is a dimer, and it brings two receptors together.

10
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:48.863
Their kinase domains then phosphorylate each other, and that starts two survival

11
00:00:48.863 --> 00:00:49.863
branches.

12
00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:55.717
The second kind, p75, binds all four neurotrophins but has no kinase.

13
00:00:56.237 --> 00:01:00.737
It belongs to the tumor necrosis factor receptor family, like the death receptor

14
00:01:00.737 --> 00:01:05.077
Fas. Like Fas, it carries a death domain inside the cell.

15
00:01:05.897 --> 00:01:08.397
Trk receptors are locks cut for certain keys.

16
00:01:08.937 --> 00:01:11.437
p75 is a doorbell that any key can ring.

17
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.520
Like most secreted proteins, NGF is made as a longer chain.

18
00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:21.200
The extra stretch at its front is the pro -domain, and the longer chain is called

19
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.360
pro -NGF. Cells can trim the pro -domain inside.

20
00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:32.300
In 2001, Hempstead and colleagues reported that cells also secrete pro -NGF uncut.

21
00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:37.500
Outside, plasmin and particular matrix metalloproteinases can cut it.

22
00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:45.460
In their experiments, uncut pro -NGF bound p75 tightly and activated track A very

23
00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:50.960
little. It triggered apoptosis of cultured sympathetic neurons through p75.

24
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:57.760
For this death signal, p75 needs a partner, sortilin, which binds the pro -domain.

25
00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:04.220
Mature NGF kept the same kind of neuron alive through track A. Another group found

26
00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:08.900
that uncut pro -NGF can also keep these neurons alive, more weakly.

27
00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:13.473
Three things go a long way toward setting what one neurotrophin does.

28
00:02:14.053 --> 00:02:18.333
Was the factor cut, which receptors does the cell make, and how much of each?

29
00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:23.353
How much precursor killing adds to the normal deaths of development is less clear.

30
00:02:23.953 --> 00:02:29.213
Cut or uncut, and which receptors: together they go a long way toward setting what

31
00:02:29.213 --> 00:02:30.033
the factor says.
